# Twenty-two metal where there is room for twenty, a turn ends, and twenty are left.
#
# **`lose-what-is-not-kept` is the turn's first part**, which is the order `spec/turn.md` states:
# upkeep, then growth or starvation, then *what expires expires, and what was not kept in order is
# lost*, then what nature reclaims, and time restoring the counts last. **Only this one and the
# refreshes are built**, and the tree in `tree.txt` is where the order can be read.
#
# **Nothing says which two metal went.** A place holds one number for a kind, so there is no metal
# in disorder to pick out - the number is bounded and what is above the bound is gone. Sean,
# 2026-09-17: *we only lose what we don't have the storage for, without tracking what is stored
# where.*
#
# **The refreshes do nothing here**, because nothing in this world carries a `moving` or a
# `working` to restore. That is `put` being a no-op where nothing matches, and it is why the turn
# can be tested one part at a time.

{test name:ending-a-turn-takes-what-is-in-disorder}

{given}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{capacity of:territory for:bin what:resource per:territory} -> 4
{capacity of:bin for:resource what:resource per:territory} -> 10
{bin where:territory-1 what:metal} -> 2
{metal where:territory-1} -> 22

{when}
{end-turn}

{then}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{capacity of:territory for:bin what:resource per:territory} -> 4
{capacity of:bin for:resource what:resource per:territory} -> 10
{bin where:territory-1 what:metal} -> 2
{metal where:territory-1} -> 20
